      ":question/id": "b8f291e3-4167-5457-a081-a84205d0f43b",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Simplify $\\cos(x+120^\\circ)$ using $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$. Enter signed coefficients.\n\n{{field-1}} $\\sin x+$ {{field-2}} $\\cos x$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use $\\cos(u+v)=\\cos u\\cos v-\\sin u\\sin v$ with $u=x$ and $v=120^\\circ$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos(x+120^\\circ)&=\\cos x\\cos 120^\\circ-\\sin x\\sin 120^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\cos x\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)-\\sin x\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin x-\\frac{1}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first blank is $- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ and the second is $- \\frac{1}{2}$.",
